  "summary": "An orchestra is a large instrumental ensemble typical of classical music, which combines instruments from different families. There are typically four main sections of instruments:The string section, including the violin, viola, cello, and double bass and Harp\nThe woodwind section, including the flute, oboe, clarinet, bassoon, and occasionally saxophone\nThe brass section, including the French horn, trumpet, trombone, cornet, and tuba, and sometimes euphonium\nThe percussion section, including the timpani, snare drum, bass drum, cymbals, triangle, tambourine, tam-tam and mallet percussion instruments",
